"ai_p_gemini": "Google Gemini",
"ai_intro": "AI splits a note into separate cards and lists, spots dates and fixes misheard words. Without AI, simple rules structure your notes: a shopping list after “buy”, an event after “at 10”, priority after “urgent”, a due date after “tomorrow” - it works offline and the note text never leaves the phone.",
"ai_queue": "You can turn on several providers - Tapedo asks them in turn, in the order of this list. When one uses up its daily limit, the next notes go to the next one. When nobody answers, the no-AI rules structure the note.",
"ai_free": "Free",
"ai_paid": "Paid per use",
"ai_on": "On",
"ai_off": "Off",
"ai_unfold": "Show",
"ai_fold": "Hide",
"ai_p_groq_hint": "The best of the free ones: decent and very fast, but misses subtleties. About 1000 requests a day per model (Nov 2026).",
"ai_p_openrouter_hint": "Very weak and makes things up (adds things that were never said) - a fallback only. “openrouter/free” picks a different model each time, so results are uneven. About 50 requests a day (Nov 2026).",
"ai_p_anthropic_hint": "The most accurate. Recommended: Claude Sonnet 5.5 - about 0.6 US cents per minute of recording (Nov 2026). Opus 5.5 costs twice as much, which is overpaying for sorting notes; the cheaper Haiku is wrong more often.",
"ai_p_openai_hint": "Default gpt-6-luna - cheap, but wrong more often. Key from the OpenAI platform.",
"ai_p_gemini_hint": "Default Gemini Flash-Lite - cheap, but wrong more often. Google gives its free plan only to some accounts and projects. Key from Google AI Studio.",
"ai_what_title": "What it is",
"ai_privacy_title": "Where your data goes",
"ai_groq_what": "A service that runs open AI models very fast. It splits a note into separate tasks and lists. The free plan needs no payment card; it has per-minute and per-day request limits.",
"ai_openrouter_what": "One account for many AI models from different companies. It splits a note into separate tasks and lists. Free models have “:free” in the name - about 50 requests a day without topping up.",
"ai_anthropic_what": "Claude AI models by Anthropic. They split a note into separate tasks and lists. Paid per use - the account needs credit; with Sonnet 5.5 roughly 0.6 US cents per minute of recording (Nov 2026).",
"ai_openai_what": "GPT AI models by OpenAI. They split a note into separate tasks and lists. Paid per use - the account needs credit.",
"ai_gemini_what": "Google’s AI model. It splits a note into separate tasks and lists and fixes misheard words. Google gives its free plan only to some accounts and projects - new projects usually work only with billing set up, which is why Gemini is paid here and last on the list. Adults only (18+).",
"ai_groq_privacy": "Only the note text goes to Groq (USA) - no data about you; the recording only if you pick Groq for Whisper. Under its terms Groq may not use it to train models. By default it stores no requests; for outages it may keep logs for up to 30 days - this can be turned off in the Groq console (Data Controls, Zero Data Retention).",
"ai_openrouter_privacy": "Only the note text goes to OpenRouter (USA) - no recording, no data about you. OpenRouter itself stores no requests unless you turn that on, but it passes them to the company running the model - with free models some of them may train on the text. Such models can be turned off in OpenRouter’s privacy settings; do not dictate sensitive data there (as of Nov 2026).",
"ai_anthropic_privacy": "Only the note text goes to Anthropic (USA) - no recording, no data about you. Under its commercial terms Anthropic does not train models on API data and deletes requests automatically within 30 days - longer only for those flagged as breaking its rules (as of Nov 2026).",
"ai_openai_privacy": "Only the note text goes to OpenAI (USA) - no data about you; the recording only if you pick OpenAI for Whisper. API data is not used to train models unless you opt in; OpenAI keeps it for up to 30 days to detect abuse (as of Nov 2026).",
"ai_gemini_privacy": "Only the note text goes to Google - no recording, no data about you. On the paid plan Google does not use it to improve its products and keeps it for a limited time only to detect abuse. On the free plan (if your project has one), outside the EEA, Switzerland and the UK, Google may use the text and let people read it - then do not dictate sensitive data (as of Nov 2026).",
"ai_how_key": "How to get a key",
"ai_get_key": "Create a key",
"ai_how_groq_1": "Tap “Create a key” - the Groq console opens. Create an account (e-mail, Google or GitHub).",
"ai_how_groq_2": "In “API Keys” tap “Create API Key”, name it and copy the key - Groq shows it only once.",
"ai_how_groq_3": "Paste the key below and tap “Check connection”. The free plan needs no card.",
"ai_how_openrouter_1": "Tap “Create a key” - OpenRouter opens. Create an account.",
"ai_how_openrouter_2": "In “Keys” tap “Create Key”. Under “Credit limit” choose “Custom amount” and enter 1 - it only caps what the key may spend; without topping up the account you pay nothing, and “:free” models cost 0. Copy the key - it is shown only once.",
"ai_how_openrouter_3": "Pick a model with “:free” in the name - only those are free (about 50 requests a day without topping up). Paste the key below and tap “Check connection”.",
"ai_how_anthropic_1": "Tap “Create a key” - the Claude console opens. Create an account.",
"ai_how_anthropic_2": "In “Billing” add credit - without it the key does not work.",
"ai_how_anthropic_3": "In “API keys” tap “Create Key”, copy the key (shown only once), paste it below and tap “Check connection”.",
"ai_how_openai_1": "Tap “Create a key” - the OpenAI platform opens. Create an account.",
"ai_how_openai_2": "In “Billing” add credit - without it the key does not work.",
"ai_how_openai_3": "In “API keys” tap “Create new secret key”, copy the key (shown only once), paste it below and tap “Check connection”.",
"ai_how_gemini_1": "Tap “Create a key” - Google AI Studio opens. Sign in with a Google account.",
"ai_how_gemini_2": "On aistudio.google.com/billing set up billing for the project - without it Gemini works only in projects with a free plan (see the “Billing Tier” column; “Free tier unavailable” = paid only).",
"ai_how_gemini_3": "Tap “Create API key”, copy the key, paste it below and tap “Check connection”.",
